<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BIL Australia sets A$200 mln bond - ANZ.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BIL Australia sets A$200 mln bond - ANZ.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>BIL (Australia Finance) Ltd, a wholly owned subsidiary of Brierley Investments Ltd, has issued a A$200 million bond at 77.5 basis points over Australian Treasury bonds, lead manager ANZ Bank said.  </p>
<p>The bonds mature on March 15, 2002 and carry a coupon of 8.10 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds, which are guaranteed by the parent company, are launched off the issuer's A$500 million MTN programme.</p>
</text>
